y net into a silent-failure machine.\n- **If your own AC gate failed on a SIBLING job's in-flight file — not your own change — say so with the right verdict, not a lying FAIL.** When you are running in a shared or WIP-carrying tree (the prompt discloses this in a `--- FOREIGN WORKING-TREE STATE ---` section, if present) and your gate failure is confined to paths that section already told you are not your work, print `SCHEDULER_VERDICT: BLOCKED_BY_FOREIGN_WIP` (and `exit 1`) instead of `FAIL`, followed by a `FOREIGN_WIP_PATHS: <path1>, <path2>, ...` line naming exactly the failing paths. The scheduler independently validates every listed path against the exact manifest it disclosed to you — list a path you were never told is foreign, or claim this verdict for a regression you actually introduced, and the whole verdict is downgraded straight back to `FAIL`, rejected. This is not an escape hatch: it exists so a correctly-diagnosed \"not my regression\" outcome gets auto-requeued once the sibling clears its WIP, instead of triggering a fix-plan investigation into someone else's unfinished work.\n","numLines":98,"startLine":1,"totalLines":98}}}
