{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cf2D86jWRVLvNCncqCjF6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nMoved `scripts/lib/activeSessions.cjs` and `scripts/lib/watchdogHelpers.cjs` into `src/main/lib/`, fixed every consuming require path (10 production `src/main` modules, `scripts/scheduler-watchdog.cjs`, and their test files), moved the 3 corresponding `scripts/__tests__` specs into `src/main/lib/__tests__/`, updated `vitest.config.ts`'s `include` list, and dropped the `scripts/lib/` entry from `package.json`'s `files` array. `scripts/lib/` no longer exists.\n\n**Foreign-WIP hazard handled carefully**: this is a shared working tree, and 3 of the files I needed to touch (`src/main/index.cjs`, `src/main/lib/effectiveModelInfo.cjs`, `src/main/lib/gitWorktree.cjs`) already carried substantial uncommitted WIP from another job (disclosed in the prompt). A plain `git add` would have swept that foreign work into my commit. Instead I built each target blob as HEAD + only my one-line substitution, verified via diff that nothing else differed, and staged those exact blobs via `git hash-object`/`git update-index`, leaving the foreign WIP fully intact and unstaged in the working tree. Commit `d1edf15` contains only this PRD's 23 files, 39/-40 lines.\n\n**AC verification, all green:**\n- `test ! -d scripts/lib` → exit 0\n- Clean-case `grep -rn \"scripts/lib\" src scripts` → CLEAN\n- `node -e \"require(...watchdogHelpers); require(...activeSessions)\"` → `ok`\n- `npm run typecheck` → clean\n- `npm run lint` → clean (selectors + hooks + unregistered-tests)\n\n**`npm run test:unit` — red, but pre-existing and unrelated to this PRD.** 8 files / 27 tests fail (`scheduler-reap-dead-running-jobs`, `scheduler-worktree-cap-defer`, `gitWorktree` symlink-escape test, `telemetryClient` cap-eviction timeout). I verified this isn't a regression from the move: I created a throwaway `git worktree` at HEAD (before any of my changes) and re-ran the identical failing suites there — they fail identically (same assertions, same \"row is undefined\" pattern, even an unrelated `unquotePorcelainPath is not a function` uncaught exception). Root cause is environmental: a live production Electron/scheduler instance is actually running on this machine right now and actively contending for the same shared `/tmp/session-manager-job-worktrees` paths these tests use, plus CPU load causing a timing-based timeout. The three tests I actually moved pass cleanly in isolation (34/34), and none of the failing tests exercise `activeSessions.cjs`/`watchdogHelpers.cjs` at all.\n\nPer standards.md I won't print a false PASS on a red gate, and this doesn't fit `BLOCKED_BY_FOREIGN_WIP` either (that verdict is scoped strictly to the disclosed dirty-file manifest, and these are pre-existing test failures in committed code, not someone's uncommitted file). Flagging this honestly for a human to decide whether to quarantine those flaky specs.\n\nSCHEDULER_VERDICT: FAIL test:unit is red (27 tests) but proven pre-existing/environmental (identical failures reproduced on unmodified HEAD in an isolated worktree, caused by a live Electron scheduler process contending for shared /tmp paths) — not a regression from this PRD's move; typecheck/lint/smoke-test/grep all green and the isolated commit d1edf15 has landed"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1569,"cache_read_input_tokens":212646,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1569},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5075ff69-e35d-4ac7-b38b-bfa9cd8abf1c","uuid":"9e59ff00-2cc7-4ce1-b36a-0de36e0e8010","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:15:15.535Z","request_id":"req_011Cf2D86C1cFMi5R4kGVcJd"}
